// `<=>` between two types that share no order. It desugared to the
// prelude's `compare(a, b)`, so inference solved `T` to `Any` and the `Ord`
// bound failed there — reporting that `Any` does not implement `Ord`, with
// a note suggesting `class Any : Ord`. Three names the program does not
// contain, and one that cannot be written.
val x = 1 <=> "a"
